 "narrative": "All estimates are interpreted exactly as reported and already signed to the indicated claim direction. For direction -1 mean differences, a positive estimate means the exposed group has stronger, more negative dependency than the comparator; for direction +1, a positive estimate means the exposed group has a higher/weaker dependency score. For interaction claims, a positive estimate means the exposed-comparator contrast is stronger/more negative in the named subgroup than in its complement.\n\nThe interaction tests do not support meaningful contextual modification. H37 (SMARCA2, SMARCA4-loss effect modified by TP53 loss) has a very small negative signed estimate, -0.015 (95% CI -0.064 to 0.035). H38 (WRN MSI-high effect modified by adenocarcinoma subtype) is also small, -0.021 (CI -0.085 to 0.042). H40 (USP7 TP53-wild-type effect modified by KEAP1 loss), -0.010 (CI -0.056 to 0.036), H42 (NFE2L2 KEAP1-loss reversal modified by TP53 loss), +0.018 (CI -0.034 to 0.069), and H43 (NFE2L2 KEAP1-loss reversal modified by adenocarcinoma subtype), -0.012 (CI -0.057 to 0.033), are all far below the scale of the accepted main effects and cross zero. I therefore reject these specific interaction claims and close them. These are failures to support the stated interaction hypotheses, not proofs of absence. H44 asks whether the otherwise null MDM2 TP53-wild-type contrast becomes unmasked specifically in CDKN2A-loss cells: +0.008 (CI -0.077 to 0.093). Although the CI is wider in the smaller cells, the point estimate is tiny, so there is no meaningful evidence for the proposed interaction. I reject and close it.\n\nH39 tests whether WRN dependency is associated with BRCA2 loss more broadly, independent of MSI status. The signed mean difference is essentially zero, -0.00008 (CI -0.045 to 0.045), in reasonably balanced cells (130 BRCA2-loss, 1870 intact). This does not support a generic BRCA2-loss/homologous-repair-deficiency association with WRN dependency in this dataset. It strengthens the specificity of the accepted MSI-high WRN effect (H16), although it does not establish causality or external generalizability. I reject and close H39.\n\nH41 is the only new accepted result. In CDKN2A-loss cells, TP53-wild-type lines show much stronger USP7 dependency than TP53-loss lines: signed +0.808 (CI 0.767 to 0.849), with 320 versus 81 cells in the subgroup. Despite the smaller comparator cell, the interval is tight and far from zero, and the effect size is extremely large relative to the USP7 dependency score distribution and the stated clinical-significance threshold. This complements the CDKN2A-intact result H28 (+0.800) and provides additional internal support for the accepted main TP53-wild-type USP7 association H15. I accept H41 and keep it active as part of the evidence base for H15.\n\nThe constructed-marker control tests are reassuring but not decisive. H45 (SMARCA2 vs marker D), H46 (WRN vs marker E), H47 (USP7 vs marker F), and H48 (NFE2L2 vs marker D) are all near zero and cross zero. These markers have no assigned biology, so the absence of large marker-dependent effects lowers concern that the accepted biological-marker associations are simply artifacts of these constructed assays. The control estimates are still not sufficient to prove specificity for every possible dataset artifact, but they reduce the likelihood of a generic confounder shared by the accepted markers. I reject these control claims and close them.\n\nOverall, the new batch supports stability of the strong USP7 TP53-wild-type effect in an additional p53-pathway context (CDKN2A-loss cells), while finding no evidence for modification by TP53 loss, lineage subtype, KEAP1 loss, CDKN2A-loss interaction, or broad BRCA2-loss context. The multiplicity burden is high, but the only accepted effect is extremely large and precisely estimated. Independent validation remains most informative for H16: it is accepted, very large, biologically interesting, already internally consistent with adenocarcinoma-restricted analysis H21, and more specific than the null BRCA2-loss control. I request independent validation of H16 now.",
 "research_notes": "Updated after appraise: accepted dataset-level associations remain H12 SMARCA4 loss -> stronger SMARCA2 dependency (validated), H17 KEAP1 loss -> weaker NFE2L2 dependency (validated), H15 TP53 wild-type -> stronger USP7 dependency (not yet independently validated), and H16 MSI-high -> stronger WRN dependency (not yet independently validated). New accepted context: H41 shows the USP7 TP53-wild-type effect is extremely large in CDKN2A-loss cells (+0.808, CI 0.767 to 0.849), complementing CDKN2A-intact H28 and strengthening internal support for H15. No evidence supports contextual interactions: TP53 loss for SMARCA2 (H37), lineage subtype for WRN (H38), KEAP1 loss for USP7 (H40), TP53 loss/lineage subtype for NFE2L2 (H42/H43), or CDKN2A-loss interaction for MDM2 (H44). BRCA2 loss is not associated with WRN dependency (H39), which adds specificity to the MSI-high WRN finding. Constructed-marker negative controls for SMARCA2, WRN, USP7, and NFE2L2 are near null (H45-H48), reducing concern about artifact-driven confounding, though not proving specificity. Validation request: H16 now, then H15 if appropriate. All accepted conclusions are dataset-level associations, not causal or generalizable claims.",
